# Title: Suspicious PowerShell Encoded Command Patterns
# ID: b9d9cc83-380b-4ba3-8d8f-60c0e7e2930c
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-05-24
# Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1059.001
# Description: Detects PowerShell command line patterns in combincation with encoded commands that often appear in malware infection chains
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((process.command_line:* JAB* OR process.command_line:* SUVYI* OR process.command_line:* SQBFAFgA* OR process.command_line:* aWV4I* OR process.command_line:* IAB* OR process.command_line:* PAA* OR process.command_line:* aQBlAHgA*)) AND ((process.command_line:* -e * OR process.command_line:* -en * OR process.command_line:* -enc * OR process.command_line:* -enco*)) AND (((process.executable:*\\powershell.exe OR process.executable:*\\pwsh.exe)) OR ((process.pe.original_file_name:"PowerShell.Exe" OR process.pe.original_file_name:"pwsh.dll")))) AND NOT (((process.parent.executable:*C:\\Packages\\Plugins\\Microsoft.GuestConfiguration.ConfigurationforWindows\\* OR process.parent.executable:*\\gc_worker.exe*))))
